- op: discuss  # 420e
  at: '2026-10-30T02:44:42Z'  # 420e
  by: agent  # 420e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 420e
  clock: 9  # 420e
  nonce: 420e  # 420e
  message: "SATISFIED on dev 408f5950e9. Six PRs, one per language family, each with a corpus A/B whose every added edge was read:\n  #1944 Go (+265 on 6 repos), #1945 JS/TS (+174 on 6), #1946 Java+Ruby (+101/-2 on 8; the -2 were misbound this::), #1947 Rust (+197 on 5), #1948 C/C++ (+673 on 7; apt's 6 dangling C++ dispatch tables now resolve). Python needed nothing (the 06-08 note saying Python struct-field/var refs were absent was stale).\n\nFiled repro re-run on merged dev -- the 2026-10-29 matrix fixture (one file per language; fld = struct/object/dict field, var = local binding, glob = module/global binding, arr = array/slice/list element, arg = call argument), `hypergumbo survey`, exit 0, edge into each target:\n  go    calls       calls            calls       calls          calls\n  py    references  references       references  references     references\n  js    references  references       references  references     references\n  ts    references  references       references  references     references\n  java  references  references       references  references     references\n  rb    references  references       references  references     references\n  rs    references  references       references  references     references\n  c     dispatches_to calls,references references dispatches_to calls\n  cpp   references  references       references  dispatches_to  calls\n45/45 cells have an edge; before: 16 cells empty (go var/arr; js+ts var/glob/arr; java glob; rb glob; rs all 5; c glob; cpp fld/var/glob/arr).\nThe item's other named violation, Falco-style registration (vector of function pointers + push_back), on a fixture: `std::vector<void(*)(int)> table = { act_a, act_b }` -> references run->act_a, run->act_b; `actions.push_back(act_c)` -> calls run->act_c.\n\nKnown limits recorded in the PR messages (not violations of the statement, which is about extraction existing): C++ in member context does not link another file's free function (x265 `hpelcomp = sad;`), and a bare value in code tree-sitter misread (export-macro classes) is not linked; Rust `Type::f` with a non-repo Type (`String::from`) is not linked; JS useMemo/useCallback wrapper symbols are what js_ts already mints; a Yjs-style cross-line chain is not seen in JS either."  # 420e
